<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oslo</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Christiania, Kristiania</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oslo is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, at the head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslofjord">Oslofjord</a>. Founded in the 11th century, it became the royal capital around 1300. After a fire in 1624 Christian IV rebuilt the town beside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akershus-fortress">Akershus Fortress</a> and named it Christiania; it was the seat of the Danish governors of Norway and became the capital of the independent kingdom in 1814. It took back the name Oslo in 1925.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oslo.jpg" alt="Oslo" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Orjanarvola · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nationaltheatret_evening.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
